this morning we're looking at  understanding huntington's disease one  local woman is making it her mission to  spread awareness surrounding the disease  and support for those who are dealing  with it sarah gardner's father passed  away from huntington's disease in 2015  but her battle surrounding the disease  continues huntington's disease is a  genetic disorder progressively breaking  down the nerve cells in the brain it  impacts a person's physical and mental  abilities after her dad raymond's  diagnosis sarah and her mom would turn  to local support groups to learn more  about huntington's and its symptoms  which include slurred speech involuntary  movements and so much more her dad's  symptoms even led to him being wrongly  arrested as police thought raymond was  intoxicated in public  it was a shock for sure and i said what  are you doing why are you in jail and he  said i don't know  i don't know why i'm here and  i said well what did they arrest you for  and he said public intoxication  and i was like there's no way like my  dad would never do that like it was just  totally not in his character  sarah says while she tested negative for  the disease she's still active in the  huntington's community and hopes  spreading awareness will help others in  similar situations heather
 

